{"evidence_refs":[],"id":"5eed0000-0000-0000-0000-000000000027","message":"Candidate A: teach the sizing pass about literal tabs.","metrics":{"files_changed":1.0,"lines_changed":7.0,"model_confidence":0.71},"mission_id":"b7ad2c10-4f61-4f6d-9d2e-1c7a4b6d0e11","payload":{"kind":"patch_candidate","patch":{"created_at":"2026-08-07T13:00:32Z","diff":"diff --git a/src/decode.c b/src/decode.c\n--- a/src/decode.c\n+++ b/src/decode.c\n@@ -72,6 +72,13 @@ size_t pkt_decoded_length(const uint8_t *src, size_t len, int escaped)\n             continue;\n         }\n\n+        if (c == '\\t') {\n+            /* A literal tab is expanded by pkt_decode_into(); size for it. */\n+            need += PKT_TAB_WIDTH;\n+            i += 1;\n+            continue;\n+        }\n+\n         /* Every remaining byte is copied through as-is. */\n         need += 1;\n         i += 1;\n","files_changed":1,"finding_id":"2f9a5d33-8c4b-4a1e-9f70-6b2d9e5c1a04","id":"41d0c8a7-6e35-4b92-8f4c-0d17a2e9b3f8","lines_changed":7,"mission_id":"b7ad2c10-4f61-4f6d-9d2e-1c7a4b6d0e11","model":{"captured_at":"2026-08-06T13:00:00Z","confidence":0.71,"context_bytes":4812,"model_name":"qwen2.5-coder-7b-instruct-q4","model_revision":"2026-07-11","prompt_sha256":"c2b1a0f9e8d7c6b5a4938271605f4e3d2c1b0a9988776655443322110ffee0dd","replayed_from_transcript":"transcript://pktcfg-001/candidate-a","served_from":"http://model-gateway.internal:8081","transcript_sha256":"1f2e3d4c5b6a798877665544332211000fedcba9876543210abcdef012345678"},"policy_detail":"1 file, 7 lines, inside src/ \u2014 within policy.","policy_status":"ACCEPTED","provenance":"MODEL_GENERATED","rationale":"pkt_decoded_length and pkt_decode_into must agree byte for byte. The writing pass expands a literal 0x09 to PKT_TAB_WIDTH spaces; the sizing pass counts it as one byte. Sizing for the expansion makes the allocation match what is written."}},"sequence":39,"severity":"INFO","stage":"PATCH","state":"PATCH","status":"SUCCEEDED","timestamp":"2026-08-07T13:00:24.50